---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { products } from '../../data/products';

const slugOrder = [
  'august-wifi-smart-lock-4th-gen',
  'google-nest-thermostat-2020',
  'philips-hue-starter-kit',
  'wyze-cam-v4',
  'amazon-echo-dot-5th-gen',
];

const picks = slugOrder.map(slug => products.find(p => p.slug === slug)!);
const topPick = picks[0];

const bestFor: Record<string, string> = {
  'august-wifi-smart-lock-4th-gen': 'Best Overall — No Drilling, Works on Any Deadbolt',
  'google-nest-thermostat-2020': 'Best for Energy Savings',
  'philips-hue-starter-kit': 'Best Lighting Upgrade',
  'wyze-cam-v4': 'Best Security Camera',
  'amazon-echo-dot-5th-gen': 'Best Voice Control Hub',
};
---

<Layout
  title="Best Smart Home Devices for Renters Under $300 (2025) — No Drilling, No Damage"
  description="The best smart home devices for renters under $300 total in 2025 — renter-safe picks that don't require drilling, permanent wiring, or landlord approval. Top picks from August, Nest, Philips Hue, Wyze, and Amazon."
>
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-8">

    <!-- FTC Disclosure -->
    <div class="bg-yellow-50 border border-yellow-200 rounded-md p-3 mb-6 text-sm text-yellow-800">
      <strong>Disclosure:</strong> HouseGearGuide earns a commission if you buy through our links — at no cost to you. We only recommend products we've researched thoroughly.
    </div>

    <!-- Breadcrumb -->
    <nav class="text-sm text-gray-500 mb-4">
      <a href="/" class="hover:underline">Home</a> &rsaquo;
      <a href="/smart-home/" class="hover:underline">Smart Home</a> &rsaquo;
      <span class="text-gray-700">Best Smart Home Devices for Renters Under $300</span>
    </nav>

    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Best Smart Home Devices for Renters Under $300 (2025)</h1>

    <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6">
      Renting doesn't mean you can't have a smart home — it means you need the right gear. These five devices cover the core smart home pillars — security, climate, lighting, cameras, and voice control — without drilling holes, running new wiring, or risking your security deposit. The full setup comes in under $300 and moves with you when you leave.
    </p>

    <!-- Renter Rules Box -->
    <div class="bg-blue-50 border border-blue-200 rounded-lg p-4 mb-8 text-sm text-blue-900">
      <strong>Renter-safe rules:</strong> Every pick here installs without drilling new holes, uses existing wiring (or no wiring at all), and is fully reversible. The August Smart Lock replaces your existing deadbolt thumb turn — not the lock itself. The Nest Thermostat needs a C-wire check, but installs in 30 minutes with a screwdriver. Philips Hue bulbs screw into any socket. No landlord conversation required.
    </div>

    <!-- Top Pick Box -->
    <div class="bg-green-50 border border-green-200 rounded-lg p-5 mb-8">
      <div class="text-sm font-semibold text-green-700 uppercase tracking-wide mb-1">Top Pick — Best Smart Home Device for Renters</div>
      <div class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-1">{topPick.name}</div>
      <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm mb-3">{topPick.tagline}</p>
      <div class="flex items-center gap-4">
        <span class="text-2xl font-bold text-green-700">${topPick.price}</span>
        <a href={topPick.affiliateUrl} target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener" class="bg-orange-500 hover:bg-orange-600 text-white font-semibold px-5 py-2 rounded-md text-sm transition-colors">
          View on Amazon →
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Comparison Table -->
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Quick Comparison</h2>
    <div class="overflow-x-auto mb-10">
      <table class="w-full text-sm border-collapse border border-gray-200">
        <thead class="bg-gray-100">
          <tr>
            <th class="border border-gray-200 px-3 py-2 text-left">Device</th>
            <th class="border border-gray-200 px-3 py-2 text-left">Best For</th>
            <th class="border border-gray-200 px-3 py-2 text-left">Renter Safe?</th>
            <th class="border border-gray-200 px-3 py-2 text-left">Price</th>
            <th class="border border-gray-200 px-3 py-2 text-left">Link</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {picks.map((p, i) => (
            <tr class={i % 2 === 0 ? 'bg-white' : 'bg-gray-50'}>
              <td class="border border-gray-200 px-3 py-2 font-medium">{p.name}</td>
              <td class="border border-gray-200 px-3 py-2 text-xs text-green-700 font-medium">{bestFor[p.slug]}</td>
              <td class="border border-gray-200 px-3 py-2 text-xs font-semibold text-green-700">Yes</td>
              <td class="border border-gray-200 px-3 py-2">${p.price}</td>
              <td class="border border-gray-200 px-3 py-2">
                <a href={p.affiliateUrl} target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline font-medium">Amazon →</a>
              </td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <!-- Individual Product Reviews -->
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6">Full Reviews</h2>

    {picks.map((p, i) => (
      <div class="border border-gray-200 rounded-lg p-6 mb-6">
        <div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-4 mb-3">
          <div>
            <div class="text-xs font-semibold text-green-700 uppercase tracking-wide mb-1">
              #{i + 1} — {bestFor[p.slug]}
            </div>
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900">{p.name}</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm mt-1">{p.tagline}</p>
          </div>
          <div class="text-right flex-shrink-0">
            <div class="text-2xl font-bold text-green-700">${p.price}</div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-3 text-sm mb-4">
          {Object.entries(p.specs).map(([key, val]) => (
            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded px-3 py-1.5">
              <span class="font-medium text-gray-700">{key}:</span> {val}
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>

        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mb-4">
          <div>
            <div class="font-semibold text-green-700 mb-1 text-sm">Pros</div>
            <ul class="text-sm space-y-1">
              {p.pros.map(pro => <li class="flex gap-1.5"><span class="text-green-500 mt-0.5">✓</span><span>{pro}</span></li>)}
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="font-semibold text-red-600 mb-1 text-sm">Cons</div>
            <ul class="text-sm space-y-1">
              {p.cons.map(con => <li class="flex gap-1.5"><span class="text-red-400 mt-0.5">✗</span><span>{con}</span></li>)}
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

        <a href={p.affiliateUrl} target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener" class="inline-block bg-orange-500 hover:bg-orange-600 text-white font-semibold px-5 py-2 rounded-md text-sm transition-colors">
          Check Price on Amazon →
        </a>
      </div>
    ))}

    <!-- Buying Guide -->
    <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-lg p-6 mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Renter Smart Home Buying Guide</h2>

      <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-2">The $300 Renter Smart Home Setup</h3>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto mb-4">
        <table class="w-full text-xs border-collapse border border-gray-200">
          <thead class="bg-gray-100">
            <tr>
              <th class="border border-gray-200 px-2 py-1.5 text-left">Device</th>
              <th class="border border-gray-200 px-2 py-1.5 text-left">What It Adds</th>
              <th class="border border-gray-200 px-2 py-1.5 text-left">Price</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr class="bg-white"><td class="border border-gray-200 px-2 py-1.5">August Smart Lock</td><td class="border border-gray-200 px-2 py-1.5">Keyless entry + remote lock/unlock</td><td class="border border-gray-200 px-2 py-1.5 font-medium">~$80</td></tr>
            <tr class="bg-gray-50"><td class="border border-gray-200 px-2 py-1.5">Google Nest Thermostat</td><td class="border border-gray-200 px-2 py-1.5">Energy savings + remote temp control</td><td class="border border-gray-200 px-2 py-1.5 font-medium">~$130</td></tr>
            <tr class="bg-white"><td class="border border-gray-200 px-2 py-1.5">Wyze Cam v4</td><td class="border border-gray-200 px-2 py-1.5">Indoor security + package monitoring</td><td class="border border-gray-200 px-2 py-1.5 font-medium">~$36</td></tr>
            <tr class="bg-gray-50"><td class="border border-gray-200 px-2 py-1.5">Echo Dot</td><td class="border border-gray-200 px-2 py-1.5">Voice control hub for everything</td><td class="border border-gray-200 px-2 py-1.5 font-medium">~$50</td></tr>
            <tr class="bg-white"><td class="border border-gray-200 px-2 py-1.5 font-semibold">Total</td><td class="border border-gray-200 px-2 py-1.5"></td><td class="border border-gray-200 px-2 py-1.5 font-bold text-green-700">~$296</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-2">Does the Nest Thermostat Work Without a C-Wire?</h3>
      <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm mb-4">
        The Google Nest Thermostat (2020) is one of the few smart thermostats that works without a C-wire in most installations — it uses a technique called "power stealing" from the heating/cooling wires to charge its internal battery. It's compatible with the majority of rental-unit HVAC systems. Before buying, use the Nest compatibility checker at nest.com/support to verify your system. If you have a heat pump or radiant floor heat, check first — these sometimes require a C-wire adapter.
      </p>

      <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-2">Smart Lock for Renters: What Landlords Can't Object To</h3>
      <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm mb-4">
        The August Smart Lock attaches to the interior side of your existing deadbolt — the lock cylinder and key slot outside are unchanged. Your landlord keeps their key, the building master key still works, and nothing about the exterior hardware changes. When you move out, the August unscrews in 60 seconds and your original thumb turn goes back on. It's the cleanest renter smart lock option because it doesn't replace anything — it extends what's already there.
      </p>

      <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-2">What to Buy First vs What to Add Later</h3>
      <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm mb-4">
        Start with the Echo Dot ($50) — it becomes the hub that controls everything else by voice. Add the Wyze Cam v4 ($36) if package theft or security is a concern. Add the Nest Thermostat if your apartment allows thermostat replacement (most do — it uses existing wires). Add the August Smart Lock last because it has a monthly fee for remote access beyond basic Bluetooth range. The Philips Hue kit is a nice upgrade but not essential if you're budget-constrained.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Related Guides -->
    <div class="border-t border-gray-200 pt-6">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-3">Related Guides</h2>
      <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm">
        <li>→ <a href="/smart-home/best-smart-home-devices-for-renters/" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">Best Smart Home Devices for Renters (All Budgets)</a></li>
        <li>→ <a href="/smart-home/best-smart-home-devices-under-100/" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">Best Smart Home Devices Under $100</a></li>
        <li>→ <a href="/smart-home/best-smart-home-starter-kit-under-200/" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">Best Smart Home Starter Kits Under $200</a></li>
        <li>→ <a href="/smart-home/best-smart-lock-for-renters/" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">Best Smart Locks for Renters</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>

  </div>
</Layout>
